"""General lifestyle information shown under a finding in the exam summary.

Design rules (do not relax without a clinician):
  * Text is FIXED and reviewed, never generated by the AI. The AI never writes advice here.
  * An item is shown only if it cites at least one verified source (PubMed id + DOI below).
    Items without a verified source stay in ITEMS with `sources=[]` and are hidden (TODO list).
  * Generic wording only: no doses, no personalised plan, no "you should". Everything ends
    with "talk to your doctor".
  * Off by default: env LIFESTYLE_INFO=on turns the section on. While `REVIEWED_BY` is empty
    the section carries a visible "not yet reviewed by a clinician" line.
  * Triggers are deterministic (numbers / words printed in the report), see `topics_for_exams`.

Sources were looked up in PubMed (abstracts read, DOI links kept). Scope notes matter: the exercise
review covers POSTMENOPAUSAL women, NOGG covers postmenopausal women and men >= 50. For younger
patients the texts say so and the doctor decides.
"""
